 "purpose": "The program's command-line entry point: parses the start arguments, handles the one-off commands (version, tests, shortcut, forgotten password, error log) and otherwise starts the curses app.",
 "details": "main() is called by leeravontuur.py (and `python -m leeravontuur`). Order: version/tests/shortcut/forgotten-password/error-log commands return early; --debug and LEERAVONTUUR_ZAAD (a fixed random seed for handbook screenshots) set the environment; then it imports curses and the App, builds a 'voorrang' dict from the display arguments (they win over stored settings but are not stored), checks the lock file kern/slot (a second copy asks for confirmation), opens storage, sets the locale and runs curses.wrapper(draai) so that App.start runs. A last-resort handler writes unexpected exceptions to the error log (kern/foutlog) instead of showing Python errors to the child; afterwards it closes the clock window, builds the goodbye (with the child's name and today's score) and closes storage. ESCDELAY=25 is set at import time so Esc reacts at once. Exit code 1 when the app crashed.",
 "module_docstring": "Leeravontuur starten: python3 leeravontuur.py (of python3 -m leeravontuur).",
